# Maintainable Page Objects

- One page class per route or major flow (`LoginPage`, `CheckoutPage`)
- Constructor receives `Page`; expose locators as `readonly` properties
- Methods represent **user actions** (`login()`, `addToCart()`), not test assertions
- Shared navigation lives in `BasePage.js`
- Reusable widgets (header, modal) go in `pages/components/`
- Inject page objects via Playwright fixtures — specs should not `new PageObject(page)` manually
- Update one page object when UI changes; never duplicate selectors across specs

```javascript
// Page object: action only
async submitLogin(email, password) {
  await this.emailInput.fill(email);
  await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
  await this.loginButton.click();
}

// Spec: assertion
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/account/);
```
